  - Section: papers
    Localizations:
    - Key: warning
      Text: "TO ANYONE WHO FINDS THIS,\r\n\r\nDo not explore this sector alone. The
        corridors are not secure, and something hostile is still moving through the
        facility. The upper levels were supposed to remain isolated, but the breaches
        have made that impossible to maintain.\r\nWithout a guard, you will not make
        it far. Stay near the secure zones, and do not enter any locked wing unless
        you are prepared for contact. Silence in Sector Null is never a sign of safety.\r\n\r\n\u2014
        Security Notice\r\n"
    - Key: crafting.ammo
      Text: '9MM PISTOL AMMO

        crafting guide


        Recipe for making
        10x 9mm Pistol Ammo. To make a Pistol Ammo you need to combine the following
        materials:


        5x Gunpowder

        1x Scrap'
    - Key: bloody
      Text: 'IF YOU ARE READING THIS

        DON''T LOOK BEHIND YOU'
    - Key: puzzle1
      Text: "Personal reminder \u2014 do not lose this.\n\nThe break room code follows
        the inspection order.\r\nThink of the four sections of this floor and the
        numbers assigned to each during the last safety inspection.\r\n\r\nReception:
        3rd\r\nWard A: 1st\r\nStorage: 4th\r\nGuard Post: 2nd\r\n"
    - Key: Hint1
      Text: "FACILITY SECURITY NOTICE\r\n\r\n       All restricted areas are protected
        by a \r\n       keycard access system.\r\n\r\n       LEVEL 1 \u2014 Green
        Keycard\r\n       LEVEL 2 \u2014 Red Keycard\r\n       LEVEL 3 \u2014 Master
        Keycard\r\n\r\n       Your clearance level determines which \r\n       doors
        you can open. Do NOT attempt to \r\n       force access beyond your level.\r\n\r\n      
        If you found this card \u2014 you shouldn't \r\n       be here.\r\n\n\u2014
        Security Division, Sector Null"
    - Key: BreakroomNote
      Text: 'Personal reminders do not lose this.



        The guardroom code follows
        the inspection order.

        Think of the four sections of this floor and
        the numbers assigned to each during the last safety inspection.

        Reception:
        3rd

        Ward A: 1st

        Storage: 4th

        Guard Post: 2nd


        Put
        them in order of inspection. That is the code.

'
    - Key: theaterRoomDoorNote
      Text: "TO ANYONE WHO FINDS THIS,\n\r\nThe theater room was sealed after the
        last containment failure, and no one below senior clearance was told what
        was inside. Power to the lock was split across three emergency fuses, supposedly
        to keep the section isolated, though that was never the full story.\r\nSomething
        in that room was important enough to bury, and the people in charge made
        sure it stayed buried. If you are trying to open it now, then you are already
        deeper into the facility than you should be.\n\r\n\u2014 Restricted Notice\r\n"
    - Key: OperationsRoomNote
      Text: "TO ANYONE WHO FINDS THIS,\n\r\nMaintenance record: one emergency fuse
        was moved into this operations room during the blackout and left here until
        power restoration could be attempted. The fuses are required to open the
        theater room and restore power to the locked system. If the facility loses
        power again, this section should be checked first.\n\r\nDo not assume this
        room is clear just because nothing is moving right now. The operations sector
        has been unstable since the collapse, and the structure itself is beginning
        to fail.\n\r\n\u2014 Maintenance Record\r\n"
    - Key: SecondFusePuzzleNote
      Text: "TO ANYONE WHO FINDS THIS,\n\r\nI know what they hid in the theater room,
        but every route to it was sealed behind layered mechanisms. One part is hidden
        behind the device on this floor, and the rest was scattered where nobody
        would think to search. That was deliberate.\r\nIf you are still trying to
        force your way through, stop wasting time looking blindly. The answer is
        inside the room itself.\n\r\n\u2014 Hidden Notice\r\n"
    - Key: lockpicknote
      Text: "TO ANYONE WHO FINDS THIS,\n\nI locked this room myself, hoping no one
        would ever need what was stored inside. If you find a way in continuing what
        I could not finish. To open this door, you will need a lockpick.\nI am sorry
        it came to this, but once the facility started failing, hiding things became
        easier than explaining them.\n\n\n\u2014 Private Notice\n"
    - Key: ballNote
      Text: "They used to dismiss this object as useless,\n\nbut it is not. The table
        puzzle was built around it, and without it the last fuse cannot be reached.
        That was always the trick \u2014 hide something important inside something
        that looks harmless.\r\nIf you have made it this far, do not leave it behind.
        It matters more than it looks.\r\n"
    - Key: theaterTapeNote
      Text: 'TO ANYONE WHO FINDS THIS,



        If the tape is still here, then
        nobody has time to destroy it. Watch it carefully, because it explains what
        this facility really is, what was hidden below it.

        After that, there
        will be no turning back. The truth inside Sector Null is not something they
        intended for anyone to hear.

'
    - Key: genNote
      Text: "TO ANYONE WHO FINDS THIS,\n\r\nThe facility is still running on backup
        power, and it will not hold for long. The main generator must be turned on
        before the power systems can fully function again, but it will not start
        unless fuel is brought to the operations sector first.\r\nIf you are planning
        to leave, you need to find the fuel, restore the generator, and bring the
        main systems back online. Only then will the main exit respond again \u2014
        assuming the rest of the facility does not wake up with it.\n\r\n\u2014 Maintenance
        Record\r\n"
    - Key: fuelNote
      Text: 'TO ANYONE WHO FINDS THIS,



        Emergency fuel reserves were moved
        into this room after the lower storage flooded, and they were never intended
        for regular use. They should only be touched if power restoration becomes
        necessary.

        If you are up here to turn on the generator, then time
        is already running out. Sector Null has started reacting to the blackout,
        and that is never a good sign.

'
    - Key: SafeNote
      Text: "TO ANYONE WHO FINDS THIS,\n\nThe master keycard remains with the director\u2019s
        records, locked away with the safe and the tape archive. If you want the
        code for the safe, you need to watch the tape first, because the numbers
        were never written down anywhere else.\n\nOnce you have the code, open the
        safe and take what is inside. Control failed the moment Sector Null stopped
        obeying its own systems, and the people in charge believed the facility could
        contain anything. They were wrong.\n"
    - Key: MainDoorNote
      Text: "TO ANYONE WHO FINDS THIS,\n\r\nMain gate unlock requires restored power
        and master-level access. In the event of total containment failure, all personnel
        are advised to evacuate immediately and avoid all lower sectors. If the gate
        is still open, leave now and do not look back.\r\nSector Null is no longer
        secure.\n\r\n\u2014 Final Evacuation Notice\r\n"
    - Key: StartingNote
      Text: 'TO ANYONE WHO FINDS THIS,



        Do not remain in this sector any
        longer than necessary. The lower corridor was breached first, and the containment
        line failed before anyone had time to respond.


        If I did not make
        it out, take the flashlight and leave immediately. Sector Null is no longer
        stable, and whatever is moving through the facility is getting closer by
        the minute.'
  - Section: inventory
    Localizations:
    - Key: context.use
      Text: Use
    - Key: context.examine
